    "sourceWikitext": "{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Indian recipes\n| Servings = 8\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]] | [[Cookbook:Rice Recipes|Rice]]\n\n'''Chakarai pongal''' is a sweet and buttery porridge-like dish that is traditionally prepared in South [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|India]] for the Makar Sankranti festival that heralds the arrival of summer. The [[Cookbook:Khara pongal|khara pongal]] variety differs only in the spices added, and the two are often cooked together from the same batch of rice and dhal.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] white [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Mung Bean|moong]] [[Cookbook:Dal|dhal]]\n* 4 cups [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Cashew|cashew]] nuts\n* ¼ cup white [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom]] powder\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]] (or [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]])\n* ¾ cup [[Cookbook:Jaggery|jaggery]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Cook the rice and dhal together with cups of water in a pot or [[Cookbook:Pressure Cooker|pressure cooker]] until mushy.\n# Meanwhile, melt the jaggery with 1 cup of water in a pan.\n# Add the cardamom to the jaggery as it melts.\n# Mush the rice and paruppu (dal) mixture well and add to the pan of jaggery.\n# Stir well and cook on low heat till the mixture comes together well.\n# Heat 4 tablespoons of the ghee in a separate pan and [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] cashews to golden brown. \n# Add raisins and fry for a few more seconds or until they swell up. \n# Add the nuts and raisins to into the pongal.\n# Serve hot with an additional dollop of neyyi or ghee. \n\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Holiday recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes for porridge]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cashew]]\n[[Category:Dal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using jaggery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mung bean]]",
